# Server
PORT=4000
NODE_ENV=development
JWT_SECRET=dev-secret-change-me

# Error tracking (optional — falls back to console-only logging if unset). Shared across
# all 5 services + all 7 background workers (see infra/errorTracking.ts). Get a DSN from
# sentry.io (or any Sentry-compatible self-hosted instance) for a new project.
SENTRY_DSN=

# scraper-service (the only extracted service that runs today)
SCRAPER_SERVICE_PORT=4003
SCRAPER_SERVICE_URL=http://localhost:4003

# Shared secret the gateway attaches to requests it proxies to scraper-service, so it can
# reject traffic that didn't come through the gateway. Change this for any environment where
# the service isn't behind a private network.
INTERNAL_SERVICE_KEY=dev-internal-key-change-me

# New Campaign research pipeline (marketResearch.ts): when GEMINI_API_KEY (below) is
# unset, this is used instead of the static hardcoded fallback text. Points at a local FastAPI
# service (apps/scraper-service/python/research_server.py) wrapping scrapegraphai + a local model
# — real, page-grounded extraction with no external API key required, but slower (~1-3min per URL
# on CPU) and lower-quality on inferential fields (audience/competitor/market reasoning) than the
# Gemini path. Falls back to the static fallback text if unreachable.
SCRAPEGRAPH_SERVICE_URL="http://localhost:5055"

# Meta ads adapter (optional — falls back to mock data if unset)
META_ACCESS_TOKEN=
META_AD_ACCOUNT_ID=

# Google ads adapter (optional — falls back to mock data if unset)
GOOGLE_ADS_DEVELOPER_TOKEN=
GOOGLE_ADS_CUSTOMER_ID=
GOOGLE_ADS_ACCESS_TOKEN=

# Google OAuth (optional — falls back to mock connect if unset). Create an OAuth 2.0
# Client ID (Web application) at console.cloud.google.com, and apply for/obtain a
# Google Ads developer token (GOOGLE_ADS_DEVELOPER_TOKEN above) — both are required
# for the real per-workspace connect flow, not just the legacy global-token adapter mode.
GOOGLE_OAUTH_CLIENT_ID=
GOOGLE_OAUTH_CLIENT_SECRET=
GOOGLE_OAUTH_REDIRECT_URI=http://localhost:4000/api/integrations/google/oauth/callback

# TikTok ads adapter (optional — falls back to mock data if unset)
TIKTOK_ACCESS_TOKEN=
TIKTOK_ADVERTISER_ID=

# TikTok OAuth (optional — falls back to mock connect if unset). Register an app in the
# TikTok for Business developer portal (business-api.tiktok.com/portal) to get an app ID
# and secret — note this connects the per-workspace advertiser account for account
# selection/visibility; the live ad launch above still uses TIKTOK_ACCESS_TOKEN/
# TIKTOK_ADVERTISER_ID until TikTok gets the same per-workspace hierarchy depth Meta/Google have.
TIKTOK_APP_ID=
TIKTOK_APP_SECRET=
TIKTOK_OAUTH_REDIRECT_URI=http://localhost:4000/api/integrations/tiktok/oauth/callback

# Meta OAuth (optional — falls back to mock connect if unset). Register a Meta App
# at developers.facebook.com, add "Facebook Login for Business", and set the
# redirect URI below as an allowed OAuth redirect URI on that app.
META_APP_ID=
META_APP_SECRET=
META_OAUTH_REDIRECT_URI=http://localhost:4000/api/integrations/meta/oauth/callback

# Meta Lead Ads webhook (optional — required only to receive real-time leadgen events).
# Set this to any random string and enter the same value as the "Verify Token" when
# subscribing your Meta App's webhook to the `leadgen` field at developers.facebook.com.
META_WEBHOOK_VERIFY_TOKEN=

# Shared secret sales_tech_backend (the CRM's Django backend) attaches to server-to-server
# calls at /api/crm/*, so this service can tell CRM traffic apart from the public internet.
# Deliberately separate from INTERNAL_SERVICE_KEY above — this one crosses a repo/company
# boundary and shouldn't share rotation blast-radius with the intra-monorepo services.
CRM_INTERNAL_SERVICE_KEY=

# Powers every AI feature: strategy generation, market research, insights, the strategist
# chat, and creative copy generation (optional — each falls back to a deterministic
# mock/static result if unset). The platform depends FULLY on Google Gemini as the single LLM
# backend (chat + structured tool-use + embeddings) — configured in the Gemini block below
# (GEMINI_API_KEY). Image generation (modules/generation/imageProvider.ts) is a SEPARATE, OPT-IN
# subsystem and is currently OFF: ad creatives come from MANUAL UPLOAD in the Campaign Builder.
# With generation off, an in-process mock stands in and no network call is made. The provider chain
# stays wired so adopting a generation model later is a config change, not a code change: set
# IMAGE_GENERATION_ENABLED=true, or set an image key (OPENAI_API_KEY/STABILITY_API_KEY).
# Once enabled the chain is OpenAI gpt-image-1 -> Stability -> keyless Pollinations -> an
# always-succeeds placeholder. Overridable: OPENAI_IMAGE_MODEL.
# Google Imagen was REMOVED as a provider. It was keyed off GEMINI_API_KEY — the LLM credential —
# so every deployment implicitly had an image provider configured, and the enable-check needed a
# special exception to stop configuring the LLM from switching image generation on by itself.
# GEMINI_API_KEY is now purely an LLM credential; every image key is image-only.

# Hard ceiling on COMBINED LLM token usage, enforced by infra/llmUsageBoundary.ts — a backstop
# against runaway usage (a retry storm, an unexpectedly large batch), not a cost lever. Unlike a
# per-call budget, this is a hard stop: once hit, llmRouter.ts refuses to attempt any Gemini
# call for the rest of the UTC month.
LLM_MONTHLY_TOKEN_BUDGET=5000000
# Campaign-generation research cache TTL. A completed research run for the same
# (workspace, business, url) is reused for this long before fresh research runs, so a repeat
# "generate" for the same business doesn't re-pay the 27 providers / ~50 searches / ~47 LLM
# calls. Default 604800000 (7 days). Keep <= the 14-day UI staleness horizon. Bypass
# per-request with { "forceRefresh": true } in the POST /campaigns/generate body.
CAMPAIGN_RESEARCH_CACHE_TTL_MS=604800000
# Cache quality-gate: a cached research run is only REUSED if its grounding
# (context.metadata.overallConfidence, 0-1) is >= this AND its company-identity anchor
# (context.company) is present. A degraded run (e.g. calls timed out, leaving company=null and a
# confabulated market) is treated as a cache miss and re-researched
# instead of re-served. Default 0.50; a non-finite/out-of-[0,1] value falls back to 0.50. The
# company-null check is a hard invariant and is NOT affected by this number.
CAMPAIGN_RESEARCH_MIN_CONFIDENCE=0.5
RUNWAY_API_KEY=

# 32-byte hex key used to encrypt OAuth tokens at rest (Integration.data blob).
# Generate with: node -e "console.log(require('crypto').randomBytes(32).toString('hex'))"
TOKEN_ENCRYPTION_KEY=

# Shopify product catalog — global single-store fallback (optional — falls back to mock
# catalog data if unset, and is only used when a workspace hasn't installed the app below)
SHOPIFY_STORE_DOMAIN=
SHOPIFY_ADMIN_ACCESS_TOKEN=

# Shopify app install (optional — real per-merchant OAuth; required for App Store listing).
# Create an app at partners.shopify.com, set the redirect/webhook URLs below in its
# configuration, and enable the mandatory GDPR webhooks (app/uninstalled, customers/data_request,
# customers/redact, shop/redact) pointing at /api/webhooks/shopify/*.
SHOPIFY_APP_CLIENT_ID=
SHOPIFY_APP_CLIENT_SECRET=
SHOPIFY_OAUTH_REDIRECT_URI=http://localhost:4000/api/integrations/shopify/oauth/callback

# WooCommerce product catalog (optional — falls back to mock catalog data if unset)
WOOCOMMERCE_STORE_URL=
WOOCOMMERCE_CONSUMER_KEY=
WOOCOMMERCE_CONSUMER_SECRET=

# Firecrawl (optional — every Firecrawl-backed research provider degrades to a labeled partial
# result if unset). Get a free-tier API key (1,000 credits/mo, no card required) at
# Search (optional — degrades to a labeled partial result if unset). SearXNG is now the ONLY
# web-search backend (infra/searchRouter.ts, infra/searchTaskConfig.ts) — the metered paid
# vendors Tavily and Serper were removed. Powers SearchRankingProvider, ReviewsProvider/
# SocialMediaProvider's grounded fallback, and the generic runWebSearch. Self-hosted
# metasearch — see docker-compose.yml's `searxng` service + searxng/settings.yml. Point this
# at wherever that container is reachable. No per-call quota. Note: SearXNG applies its own
# relevance ranking, so SearchRankingProvider's `position` field is approximate (not exact
# Google rank order, which the removed Serper provided).
SEARXNG_BASE_URL=http://localhost:8888

# Crawl / content extraction (optional — degrades to in-house-only if unset). crawl4ai is now
# the ONLY external crawl backend (Firecrawl, the metered vendor, was removed). It runs
# CONCURRENTLY with the in-house Playwright scraper (scraper-service) and their results are
# merged — see infra/scrapeFallback.ts + infra/crawl4aiClient.ts. Self-hosted, no per-call
# quota — see docker-compose.yml's `crawl4ai` service. Point this at wherever that container
# is reachable.
CRAWL4AI_BASE_URL=http://localhost:11235
# Optional bearer token — set only if you started crawl4ai with auth required. Leave empty on
# a private network.
CRAWL4AI_API_TOKEN=

# Meta Ad Library API (optional — AdLibraryProvider skips the Meta source if unset; Google
# Ads Transparency Center coverage via the crawl layer still runs). Register a Meta developer
# app at developers.facebook.com and generate an access token with ads_read/public access to
# the ads_archive endpoint.
META_AD_LIBRARY_ACCESS_TOKEN=

# Where OAuth round-trips redirect the browser back to (gateway/webAppUrl.ts). Leave EMPTY unless
# the SPA is served from a different origin than the API — it falls back to PUBLIC_ORIGIN, which is
# already this deployment's browser-facing origin. If BOTH are unset it falls back to the Vite dev
# server (http://localhost:5173), which is correct locally and wrong in every deployment: every
# OAuth redirect, success and failure alike, would send the user to an address that doesn't exist
# for them.
WEB_APP_URL=

# Per-task LLM assignment (infra/llmTaskConfig.ts, infra/llmRouter.ts) — every task runs on
# Gemini. Pin a specific task to a different Gemini model without a code change via
# LLM_TASK_<TASK_NAME>="gemini:model" (see llmTaskConfig.ts's doc comment), e.g.
# LLM_TASK_STRATEGY_AGENT="gemini:gemini-pro-latest".
# A stale "bedrock:..." value here is IGNORED (the provider no longer exists) and the task falls
# back to GEMINI_MODEL rather than failing — worth knowing if an old deployment env is carried over.

DATABASE_URL="postgresql://postgres:postgres@localhost:5432/adgo?schema=public"

# Redis (docker-compose service; not yet wired into the app — reserved for Phase 1 caching/job queue)
REDIS_URL="redis://localhost:6379"

# ── Google Gemini — the SINGLE LLM backend for the whole pipeline ──
# GEMINI_API_KEY is an AI Studio API key. Powers chat, structured tool-use (forced function
# calling), and embeddings (Research Memory / RAG). Nothing in the pipeline works without it.
GEMINI_API_KEY=
# NOTE ON MODEL IDS: some pinned versions report a quota limit of 0 on AI Studio keys while the
# `-latest` aliases carry real working quota, so the default is an alias. Only pin a version after
# confirming it has quota on YOUR key, or every research leg silently returns null.
GEMINI_MODEL=gemini-flash-latest
# Embeddings for Research Memory / RAG. 1024 dims matches the stored vector width, so this can be
# changed without a schema change — BUT vectors from a different model are mathematically
# incomparable to existing ones, so changing the model means re-embedding:
#   npx tsx apps/api/src/scripts/reembedResearchMemory.ts --yes
GEMINI_EMBEDDING_MODEL=gemini-embedding-001
GEMINI_EMBEDDING_DIMENSIONS=1024
# Gemini's quotas are PER-MINUTE and the research pipeline fans out ~45 calls at once. The
# concurrency cap plus 429-backoff is what keeps a burst from failing whole research legs; raise
# the cap only if your key's per-minute quota genuinely allows it.
GEMINI_MAX_CONCURRENCY=4
GEMINI_MAX_RETRIES=6
GEMINI_MAX_BACKOFF_MS=30000
# Thinking-token allowance, added ON TOP of each caller's maxTokens. Gemini's models reason before
# answering and those thought tokens are drawn from the SAME maxOutputTokens budget as the answer —
# so without this a tight maxTokens gets spent entirely on thinking and the call returns NO output
# (finishReason=MAX_TOKENS, no parts). That is an empty SUCCESS, not an error, and the pipeline reads
# empty as "this leg produced nothing", so it degrades quality silently. Keeping thinking on its own
# allowance means a caller's maxTokens is entirely available for visible output.
# Set to 0 to send no cap and let the model budget its own thinking (then tight callers can starve).
# NOTE: you cannot disable thinking — thinkingBudget:0 is rejected with HTTP 400 on these models.
GEMINI_THINKING_BUDGET=1024

# ── Object storage (uploaded images, generated creatives, crawl artifacts) ────────────────────
# Absolute directory for stored blobs, served back at /objects/<key>. Leave UNSET for local dev —
# it defaults to apps/api/data/objects, resolved relative to the module.
#
# Set it explicitly in a container. The built image copies apps/api/dist to /repo/service/dist, so
# the default resolves to /repo/service/data/objects, one level shallower than the repo layout
# suggests. Relying on that derivation is how uploads previously ended up written to the container's
# ephemeral layer instead of the mounted volume and disappeared on every rebuild — so the deployment
# states the path outright (see OBJECT_STORAGE_DIR in docker-compose.yml) and mounts a volume there.
# Every container that WRITES objects needs that same mount, or the api cannot read back a key a
# worker produced.
OBJECT_STORAGE_DIR=
